            <ArticleTitle>Perforated gastric ulcer in children. Case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>182-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>12-year-old boy in whom a benign gastric ulcer perforated into the free abdominal cavity is reported. He has underwent emergency operation with a preoperative diagnosis of acute peritonitis due to perforation of peptic ulcer. Gastric ulcer is a rare disease of childhood. The illness was discussed in view of the literature.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
